 big fan of the new Geneses. If you look to mythology itself, there are plenty of awesome characters caught up in things without being the blood relations of the gods, and at the table more options can only be a good thing. The chance to play a Scion of Anubis who was carved from stone as a slave ushabti but has unexpected free will or a normal guy killed and Chosen by The Dagda to return from the dead as his servant are both just as interesting (if not more so!) than &quot;Zeus was secretly my dad.&quot; My only complaint is that the Incarnates are all the way back in God, because that's super rich ground to work with.<br /> <br /> Obviously they'll have mechanics, or else the Incarnates wouldn't have been pushed back to a later book. They also inform one of your Paths, which are technically mechanical effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}